Move a floating group to another monitor once, not once per window

Moving a workspace to another monitor, or swapping two monitors' active
workspaces, translates each floating window on it by the offset between the
monitors. It does so through the window's layout target, and every window
in a group returns the group's shared target, so a floating group was
translated once for every window in it. A floating group of two windows
moved from one monitor to the next landed one monitor's width past it, off
every screen, which left the workspace looking empty on its new monitor.

Translate each layout target once per move.

Not yet upstream.

--- a/src/state/workspace/PlacementController.cpp
+++ b/src/state/workspace/PlacementController.cpp
@@ -26,9 +26,21 @@
 #include "../../workspace/query/Query.hpp"
 
 #include <ranges>
+#include <vector>
 
 using namespace State::Workspace;
 
+// The windows of a group share the group's layout target, so translating the target once per window
+// would move a floating group by the offset once for every window in it.
+static void translateFloatingTarget(const PHLWINDOW& w, const Vector2D& offset, std::vector<SP<Layout::ITarget>>& translated) {
+    const auto TARGET = w->layoutTarget();
+    if (!w->isFloating() || !TARGET || std::ranges::contains(translated, TARGET))
+        return;
+
+    translated.emplace_back(TARGET);
+    TARGET->setPositionGlobal(TARGET->position().translate(offset));
+}
